p>
<p><img alt=3D"e310" src=3D"https://antsdr-docs.microphase.cn/en/latest/_im=
ages/20bbee3df177e2c2145119c01b767951.jpg" width=3D"696.4479370117188" heig=
ht=3D"691.6771240234375"></p>
<p data-imt-p=3D"1">At this time, the user takes out his mobile phone, turn=
s on wifi and should be able to search for a device called openwif.<font cl=
ass=3D"notranslate immersive-translate-target-wrapper" lang=3D"zh-CN" data-=
imt-deferred-display=3D"" style=3D"display: none;"><br><font class=3D"notra=
nslate immersive-translate-target-translation-theme-none immersive-translat=
e-target-translation-block-wrapper-theme-none immersive-translate-target-tr=
anslation-block-wrapper" data-immersive-translate-translation-element-mark=
=3D"1"><font class=3D"notranslate immersive-translate-target-inner immersiv=
e-translate-target-translation-theme-none-inner" data-immersive-translate-t=
ranslation-element-mark=3D"1">=E6=AD=A4=E6=97=B6=EF=BC=8C=E7=94=A8=E6=88=B7=
=E6=8B=BF=E5=87=BA=E6=89=8B=E6=9C=BA=EF=BC=8C=E6=89=93=E5=BC=80 wifi=EF=BC=
=8C=E5=BA=94=E8=AF=A5=E8=83=BD=E5=A4=9F=E6=90=9C=E7=B4=A2=E5=88=B0=E5=90=8D=
=E4=B8=BA openwif =E7=9A=84=E8=AE=BE=E5=A4=87=E3=80=82</font></font></font>=
</p>
<p><img alt=3D"e310" src=3D"https://antsdr-docs.microphase.cn/en/latest/_im=
ages/e728bd543ac576bacb0b542fe9dd3cf3.png" width=3D"696.4479370117188" heig=
ht=3D"647.375"></p>
<p data-imt-p=3D"1">At this stage, the WiFi network does not have Internet =
access. However, once connected, users can open the built-in OpenWiFi webpa=
ge. When connected to OpenWiFi, users can enter 192.168.13.1 in the browser=
 to open the built-in web page of OpenWiFi.</p>
<p data-imt-p=3D"1">If the user wants to connect to the Internet through Op=
enWiFi running on ANTSDR, the user needs to have a Linux computer, use an E=
thernet cable to connect ANTSDR E310 to the network port of the Linux compu=
ter, and then enter the following command in the Linux system terminal</p>
<div class=3D"highlight-default notranslate"><div class=3D"highlight"><pre>=
<span></span><span class=3D"n">sudo</span> <span class=3D"n">sysctl</span> =
<span class=3D"o">-</span><span class=3D"n">w</span> <span class=3D"n">net<=
/span><span class=3D"o">.</span><span class=3D"n">ipv4</span><span class=3D=
"o">.</span><span class=3D"n">ip_forward</span><span class=3D"o">=3D</span>=
<span class=3D"mi">1</span>
<span class=3D"n">sudo</span> <span class=3D"n">iptables</span> <span class=
=3D"o">-</span><span class=3D"n">t</span> <span class=3D"n">nat</span> <spa=
n class=3D"o">-</span><span class=3D"n">A</span> <span class=3D"n">POSTROUT=
ING</span> <span class=3D"o">-</span><span class=3D"n">o</span> <span class=
=3D"n">NICY</span> <span class=3D"o">-</span><span class=3D"n">j</span> <sp=
an class=3D"n">MASQUERADE</span>
<span class=3D"n">sudo</span> <span class=3D"n">ip</span> <span class=3D"n"=
>route</span> <span class=3D"n">add</span> <span class=3D"mf">192.168.13.0<=
/span><span class=3D"o">/</span><span class=3D"mi">24</span> <span class=3D=
"n">via</span> <span class=3D"mf">192.168.10.122</span> <span class=3D"n">d=
ev</span> <span class=3D"n">ethX</span>=20
</pre></div>
</div>
<p data-imt-p=3D"1"><code class=3D"docutils literal notranslate"><span clas=
s=3D"pre">NICY</span></code> refers to the network interface on the user=E2=
=80=99s computer that provides Internet access (e.g., <code class=3D"docuti=
ls literal notranslate"><span class=3D"pre">wlan0</span></code>). <code cla=
ss=3D"docutils literal notranslate"><span class=3D"pre">ethX</span></code> =
is the Ethernet interface connected to the ANTSDR.</p>
<p data-imt-p=3D"1">Example:</p>
<div class=3D"highlight-default notranslate"><div class=3D"highlight"><pre>=
<span></span><span class=3D"n">sudo</span> <span class=3D"n">sysctl</span> =
<span class=3D"o">-</span><span class=3D"n">w</span> <span class=3D"n">net<=
/span><span class=3D"o">.</span><span class=3D"n">ipv4</span><span class=3D=
"o">.</span><span class=3D"n">ip_forward</span><span class=3D"o">=3D</span>=
<span class=3D"mi">1</span>
<span class=3D"n">sudo</span> <span class=3D"n">iptables</span> <span class=
=3D"o">-</span><span class=3D"n">t</span> <span class=3D"n">nat</span> <spa=
n class=3D"o">-</span><span class=3D"n">A</span> <span class=3D"n">POSTROUT=
ING</span> <span class=3D"o">-</span><span class=3D"n">o</span> <span class=
=3D"n">wlan0</span> <span class=3D"o">-</span><span class=3D"n">j</span> <s=
pan class=3D"n">MASQUERADE</span>
<span class=3D"n">sudo</span> <span class=3D"n">ip</span> <span class=3D"n"=
>route</span> <span class=3D"n">add</span> <span class=3D"mf">192.168.13.0<=
/span><span class=3D"o">/</span><span class=3D"mi">24</span> <span class=3D=
"n">via</span> <span class=3D"mf">192.168.10.122</span> <span class=3D"n">d=
ev</span> <span class=3D"n">eth0</span>
</pre></div>
</div>
<p data-imt-p=3D"1">At this point, you can use your mobile phone to connect=
 to OpenWiFi and then connect to the Internet through OpenWiFi. This enable=
s the ANTSDR E310 to function as a basic WiFi router with Internet access.<=
/p>
